==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 4~13.33 seconds<sup>120f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
**2 [[Angelic Sleipnir]]s spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**3 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 2~12 seconds<sup>60f~360f</sup>.
**1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns.
**3 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**1 [[Kory]] spawns.
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns.
**10 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to the varying types of enemies this level produces, you have to use ''very different'' tactics as this level progresses.

It is easy to stall the beginning Pigeon de Sables for money, since they pose no threat on their own. Once you have enough money, you can begin to spawn your attackers and hit the base. Be wary when using units with under 467.5 range, as the Pigeon de Sables will be able to reach them with wave attacks. Once the base is damaged, many different enemies are set to appear at the same time, but only a few of them will end up spawning due to the enemy limit. This initial wave of enemies will consist of Dark Emperor Nyandam, Kory, Camelle, one Rain D., and a few Pigeon de Sables. Here it is best to use [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or another [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|wave blocker]] along with units that outrange Rain D., such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]]. The latter two also outrange the Angelic Sleipnirs. Once the initial threats are down, the other enemies will begin to spawn. They should not be difficult to kill if you have a large enough stack of midrangers.

It is also possible to delay the first Rain D. by triggering the base while a Pigeon de Sable is still alive. This is most easily pulled off using units with low damage per hit.

Due to the high speed of Rain D. and the Pigeon de Sables, they can be lured near your base and destroyed by a well-timed [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Doing so will make the remaining enemies significantly easier to fight.

